# Release-critical markdown: prettier rewrites `[comment]: <> (START OF GITHUB README)` into
# `[comment]: <> 'START OF GITHUB README'`. The Makefile slices the published README between those
# markers (`perl -ne 'print if /START OF GITHUB README/../END OF GITHUB README/'` over src/README.md,
# applied to the root copy), so a rewrite desynchronises the two files and mis-slices npm/README.md.
README.md

# Config files prettier would reformat on every `make prettier -w` run. Rewriting
# .pre-commit-config.yaml mid-commit is fatal: `pre-commit run` then aborts with
# "Your pre-commit configuration is unstaged" and the commit fails. Markdown style is owned by
# markdownlint-cli2, not prettier.
.ci-package.json
.markdownlint-cli2.yaml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
